> User bellabride2018 (287346)
array (
  '/REST/users/messenger/addReply?SessionId' => '436571b76529e28fa6564b7fd4af93dd',
  'module' => 'REST',
  'section' => 'run',
  'request_method' => 'post',
  'app' => 'REST_Service',
  'application' => 'users',
  'class' => 'messenger',
  'operation' => 'addReply',
  'SessionId' => '436571b76529e28fa6564b7fd4af93dd',
  'conversationId' => '13948',
  'messageContent' => 'Hello TD2018!

Congratulations!!
For my save the dates I sent them out last week via email.  I find the save the date is just a heads up to what is coming.  It doesnt have exact information on it.
Mine said "Pack Your Bags and Save the Date".

If your family and friends are like mine, they are all going to want to be there.  Unfortunately if I dropped this on them a year to 10 months before none of them would be able to afford to go.

So my save the date is more like a start daving your pennies now situation.  

I am also using it to confirm everyones personal information by having them email me and confirm their personal information.  That way when I am ready to send the invites out I am not scrambling for information, and I also will have everything my TA needs.

',
  'sessionId' => '436571b76529e28fa6564b7fd4af93dd',
)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
